# pool_edge -- a bullnose coping ring round the Oval. Placed in island.txt at the pool's own
# centre and at the deck's top, so these are local coordinates about the middle of the water.
#
# The pool is an ellipse and a 1 m coping run is straight, so the ring is twenty-four chords: each
# is scaled to its own chord and turned so its rounded edge overhangs the water. The turn uses the
# ellipse's true normal rather than its radius -- on an ellipse those are not the same direction,
# and using the radius is what makes a ring of coping look like a ring of dropped slabs.
# They all share one mesh and one texture, so the whole ring is a single instanced draw.
piece models/own/arch/pool_coping_run.obj    9.043  0.000   0.738   1.553 1.000 1.000   78.0 0.0 0.0   1.77 1.96 2.26  tex paving_stone 0.8
piece models/own/arch/pool_coping_run.obj    8.427  0.000   2.163   1.703 1.000 1.000   56.2 0.0 0.0   1.77 1.96 2.26  tex paving_stone 0.8
piece models/own/arch/pool_coping_run.obj    7.236  0.000   3.440   1.936 1.000 1.000   38.9 0.0 0.0   1.77 1.96 2.26  tex paving_stone 0.8
